@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] contracts-never-weakened
A contract MUST NOT be deleted, loosened or reworded to make code pass. When behaviour
changes on purpose, the contract changes in the same pull request, and its prose says
which decision changed it. A known violation is named in the pull request that finds it
until the code is fixed. "All these things that I've been saying over all these videos
have to be in contracts ... so we do not make the same mistakes" (recording 15 Oct 13:54,
07:13; K15).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] contracts-cite-their-source
A contract written from Tavi's feedback MUST name where it came from in its prose: the
recording and the time, the point (F, H, J or K numbers of the design notes) or the
`android/DESIGN.md` rule. A contract with no traceable source is a guess and is not added.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] contracts-live-by-their-code
A rule about one directory's code MUST live in the `CONTRACTS` file of that directory (or
the nearest one above it); Kotlin and Vue rules always go in a `CONTRACTS` file, since
`cc-check` does not read those languages. Every `CONTRACTS` file MUST pass
`pnpm run contracts:check`: a directive per contract, an `owner` and a `label` on each,
non-empty prose, and an ID used once in its file and in every `CONTRACTS` file above it.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] contracts-readable-in-app
Every `CONTRACTS` file in the repository MUST reach the Android app at build time and be
listed on the UI Book's Contracts page, sorted by area, with nothing left out or edited
by hand. Adding a `CONTRACTS` file needs no other change for it to show there
(message 15 Oct, "a section under the UI book for code contracts").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] phone-api-one-account
The legacy private phone API (`POST /api/rpc` and `GET /android/*`) stays behind Cloudflare Access with
the headers the phone is given in Settings, as before. The phone signs in once and stays
signed in until Sign out: with Google (see `google-sign-in-same-account`), or with email and
password for the one test account seeded from the environment. Nobody can make an account
with a password in that compatibility flow. The account's own methods (its keys,
synced settings and posted diffs) MUST need that session; the rest of the phone API is
reached as before. This replaces "no login" by Tavi's decision of 16 Oct 12:40 and 12:47
(plan "Posted diffs"); Google accounts and the password kept for test users are his of
16 Oct 16:52. Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 any-account GitHub and anonymous browsing decision adds
separate guest and personal principals; it MUST NOT broaden the legacy private API's
ingress or adopt its shared operator GitHub credential. Anonymous native browsing MAY
use fixed tokenless public GitHub REST reads. Personal GitHub sign-in MUST use a
server-owned authorization flow (GitHub CLI device sign-in since Tavi's 23 Oct 13:36
"what you get when you use GH auth login"), verified immutable GitHub identity and the user's own
isolated credential/state. Existing Google accounts MUST remain compatible; email
matching alone MUST NOT link a personal GitHub identity to an existing account.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] google-sign-in-same-account
Google sign-in makes the email's account the first time and signs in to it after, with no
step to create it, and MUST be refused, with no account made, for every email but
tocanoctavian@gmail.com and addresses at @octaviantocan.com (Tavi, 16 Oct 16:52: "The
Google sign-in should be restricted to tocanoctavian@gmail.com and emails with a
@octaviantocan.com domain"). The server MUST check the Google ID token's signature against
Google's keys, its issuer, that it was made out to the server's web client ID
(`PULLY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`) and has not expired, and that its email is verified; anything
else is refused with no session. Google-created accounts have no password unless that same email is explicitly
configured as the environment-seeded test account. Without that client ID the server takes no Google sign-in and the phone shows no Google button.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] agent-api-needs-a-key
The account-key agent API `/api/v1/*` may sit outside Cloudflare Access, and it
MUST answer 401 to every call without a valid account key, whatever the path's case or
doubled slashes (`/API/v1`, `//api//v1`; Tavi, 16 Oct 14:32). A key reaches only its own
account's posted diffs and its feedback: no phone method, no GitHub token, no AI run, no
other account (Tavi, 16 Oct 12:47: "that endpoint doesn't really allow them to do anything
unless they pass a valid API key"). The feedback is added by Tavi's ask of 20 Oct 06:10 ("we
can then act on all my feedback later on"); a key reads it and marks it done or open, and
can do nothing else to it. Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 anonymous public-browsing decision also
permits a separately configured, default-disabled read-only public service with only
`GET /api/public/v1/capabilities`, `/api/public/v1/repositories` and
`/api/public/v1/repositories/{owner}/{repo}/pulls`. That service MUST use a tokenless
fixed GitHub origin and isolated public state, reject forwarded credentials and
arbitrary legacy RPC, and MUST NOT initialize operator account, Git, agent or AI state.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] posted-diffs-not-on-the-web
A diff an agent posted opens only in the phone app, signed in to the account. The web page
MUST NOT read one: the web RPC refuses a `posted:` target or key and hides a posted diff's
stored records and cache entries, and `/-/<id>` on the web only says to open it in the app
(Tavi, 16 Oct 14:17: "just block access for everyone. On the web, I mean. And I mean
specifically for these new agent diffs").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] account-secrets-kept-as-hashes
The server keeps the account's password only as a salted PBKDF2 hash, and its sessions and
API keys only as SHA-256 hashes. A key is shown once, when it is made; afterwards only its
name and first letters are shown. None of them MAY be written into an answer, an error, a
log line or a usage event.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] github-token-stays-on-server
The GitHub token is resolved on the server and used only there. It MUST NOT be sent to
the phone or the page, written into an answer, an error, a log, an AI prompt or a work
log, or be readable through any method the phone may call.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] secrets-come-from-the-environment
Keys for the LegacyPrivate/default paid-service capability (TypeSafe, the Pi endpoint,
model providers) come only from the server's environment; its generic engine/model
requests MUST NOT override a URL or credential. Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 per-user Claude
subscription, ChatGPT subscription and Pi endpoint decision intentionally adds separate
typed, owner-scoped provider connections: their supported setup/auth flow MAY accept that
user's own endpoint or credential into protected custody (for Pi, an encrypted
account-owned vault), never arbitrary legacy RPC. Jobs MUST name the captured
connection/revision and model, not accept arbitrary execution URLs or keys. Personal or
guest work MUST NOT inherit operator environment/CLI credentials, and missing/failed
personal authority MUST NOT silently fall back to operator credentials or paid default
use. A guest has no personal paid authority. GitHub sign-in MUST NOT be a prerequisite
for all AI; a separately verified Pully/local principal or explicitly labelled
anonymous/shared-default allowance MUST have its own credential and budget boundary and
MUST NOT impersonate a GitHub account (Tavi, 22 Oct 2026). No answer, notice, error,
Debug output or log line MAY echo a key or any part of it.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] one-look-two-clients
The web app and the phone app are one product with one look (DESIGN.md rule 106). Colours,
type, radii, shadows, icons and fonts are defined once, in the front matter of
`android/DESIGN.md`, `Lu` in `Icons.kt` and `PullsFonts`, and carried to the web by
`pnpm run android:design:update`; neither side MAY add a value of its own.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] strings-from-web-locales
The phone's strings come from the web's locale files: `android/app/src/main/assets/i18n`
MUST equal `packages/app/src/i18n/locales` byte for byte (DESIGN.md Enforcement, web). A
string is added once, at the web's locale, and copied over.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] agents-act-through-pr-tools
An AI job reads and acts on a pull request through the server's own tools (the PR tools
over MCP, the native Pi tool adapter for Pi). It MUST NOT be given a writable checkout,
the server's own files, the user's skills or a shell beyond its job folder, "so that they can't really
like mess anything up" (recording 14 Oct 19:19, 01:10 to 01:35).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] analyses-run-side-by-side
Two analyses of different pull requests MUST be able to run at the same time. No analysis
switches the branch of a checkout another job reads, and the server MUST NOT make a fresh
clone of the repository for every run (recording 14 Oct 19:19, 00:29 to 01:05).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] analytics-stays-on-our-server
Usage analytics from the phone, the web app and the server go only to our own server,
which keeps them as one NDJSON file per UTC day in its own folder. No analytics, crash or
telemetry package or third-party service MAY be added for it (message 15 Oct 20:58, "We
will track them directly on our server. No need for fancy packages").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] analytics-what-not-how-much
Analytics records what was done, never what was read or typed: no token or key, no diff,
file contents, file path, prompt, AI answer, comment, Ask message or search text. Events
carry counts, timings, enums, on or off values and a pull request's repo and number, and
`clean_event` in `backend/src/analytics.rs` enforces it on the server before any
event is written. `packages/core/src/analytics.ts` retains the shared client definitions
and cleaner (plan "Pulls analytics on our own server", Guardrails).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] analytics-can-be-turned-off
Each client has a Usage stats switch in Settings, on by default; turning it off drops
what is queued and sends nothing more. `PULLS_REVIEW_ANALYTICS=off` on the server stops it
writing anything, its own events included. Day files older than 365 days are deleted
(plan "Pulls analytics on our own server", Guardrails).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] server-backend-is-native-rust
The HTTP/RPC server, its background orchestration and local Git source provider MUST
run in Rust. Current builds and launchers MUST NOT start or fall back to TypeScript or
Node server implementations. Shared browser and Action code and external agent CLIs
remain separate runtime boundaries (Tavi, 16 Oct 2026 10:40:28 UTC,
"remove all the TypeScript backend", in the same Rust pull request).
